    shortDescription:     "The Android lifecycle is a state machine managed by the OS to optimize memory and battery usage. Activity Lifecycle States & Callbacks:\n- `onCreate()`: UI initialized, View binding inflated, ViewModel attached. Activity ",
    explanation:     "The Android lifecycle is a state machine managed by the OS to optimize memory and battery usage. Activity Lifecycle States & Callbacks:\n- `onCreate()`: UI initialized, View binding inflated, ViewModel attached. Activity ",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nThe Android lifecycle is a state machine managed by the OS to optimize memory and battery usage.\n\nActivity Lifecycle States & Callbacks:\n- `onCreate()`: UI initialized, View binding inflated, ViewModel attached. Activity is NOT visible yet.\n- `onStart()`: Activity becomes visible to user.\n- `onResume()`: Activity enters foreground and has user input focus.\n- `onPause()`: Activity partially obscured (e.g., multi-window mode, dialog popup, permission dialog) or about to transition to background. Stop animations and release exclusive camera/sensor locks.\n- `onStop()`: Activity is completely hidden from view. Heavy work, UI updates, and location updates must pause.\n- `onDestroy()`: Final callback before Activity is destroyed due to `finish()` or system recreation.\n\nFragment Lifecycle & Two-tier Architecture:\n- `onAttach()` -> `onCreate()` -> `onCreateView()` (view inflated) -> `onViewCreated()` (binding set, views wired) -> `onStart()` -> `onResume()`.\n- Reverse: `onPause()` -> `onStop()` -> `onDestroyView()` (Views torn down) -> `onDestroy()` -> `onDetach()`.\n\nModern Lifecycle-Aware APIs:\nInstead of manual cleanup in `onStop()`/`onDestroy()`, modern Android uses `LifecycleObserver`, `DefaultLifecycleObserver`, and `repeatOnLifecycle`.\n- `repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED)`: Automatically starts collecting coroutines when the UI reaches `onStart()` and cancels the coroutine when the UI drops below `onStop()`, avoiding background resource consumption and UI updates when invisible.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nThe Android lifecycle is a state machine managed by the OS to optimize memory and battery usage.\n\nActivity Lifecycle States & Callbacks:\n- `onCreate()`: UI initialized, View binding inflated, ViewModel attached. Activity is NOT visible yet.\n- `onStart()`: Activity becomes visible to user.\n- `onResume()`: Activity enters foreground and has user input focus.\n- `onPause()`: Activity partially obscured (e.g., multi-window mode, dialog popup, permission dialog) or about to transition to background. Stop animations and release exclusive camera/sensor locks.\n- `onStop()`: Activity is completely hidden from view. Heavy work, UI updates, and location updates must pause.\n- `onDestroy()`: Final callback before Activity is destroyed due to `finish()` or system recreation.\n\nFragment Lifecycle & Two-tier Architecture:\n- `onAttach()` -> `onCreate()` -> `onCreateView()` (view inflated) -> `onViewCreated()` (binding set, views wired) -> `onStart()` -> `onResume()`.\n- Reverse: `onPause()` -> `onStop()` -> `onDestroyView()` (Views torn down) -> `onDestroy()` -> `onDetach()`.\n\nModern Lifecycle-Aware APIs:\nInstead of manual cleanup in `onStop()`/`onDestroy()`, modern Android uses `LifecycleObserver`, `DefaultLifecycleObserver`, and `repeatOnLifecycle`.\n- `repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED)`: Automatically starts collecting coroutines when the UI reaches `onStart()` and cancels the coroutine when the UI drops below `onStop()`, avoiding background resource consumption and UI updates when invisible.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// Production Lifecycle Observer decoupling business logic from Activity callbacks\nclass CameraLocationTracker(\n    private val context: Context,\n    lifecycle: Lifecycle\n) : DefaultLifecycleObserver {\n\n    init {\n        lifecycle.addObserver(this)\n    }\n\n    override fun onStart(owner: LifecycleOwner) {\n        // Start listening to GPS updates when UI is visible\n        startLocationUpdates()\n    }\n\n    override fun onStop(owner: LifecycleOwner) {\n        // Stop listening to GPS updates immediately when Activity is hidden\n        stopLocationUpdates()\n    }\n\n    override fun onDestroy(owner: LifecycleOwner) {\n        // Clean up references and remove observer\n        owner.lifecycle.removeObserver(this)\n    }\n\n    private fun startLocationUpdates() { /* Register location listeners */ }\n    private fun stopLocationUpdates() { /* Unregister location listeners */ }\n}\n\n// In Activity:\nclass MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {\n    private lateinit var locationTracker: CameraLocationTracker\n\n    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {\n        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)\n        locationTracker = CameraLocationTracker(this, lifecycle)\n    }\n}\n```",
