    shortDescription:     "A modern production Android application leverages the official Jetpack Modern Android Development (MAD) ecosystem, centered around Clean Architecture and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF): 1. UI Layer:\n- Jetpack Compose: Mo",
    explanation:     "A modern production Android application leverages the official Jetpack Modern Android Development (MAD) ecosystem, centered around Clean Architecture and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF): 1. UI Layer:\n- Jetpack Compose: Mo",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA modern production Android application leverages the official Jetpack Modern Android Development (MAD) ecosystem, centered around Clean Architecture and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF):\n\n1. UI Layer:\n- Jetpack Compose: Modern declarative UI framework replacing imperative XML layouts. Enables reusable, reactive composables.\n- Material 3: Adaptive theming, dynamic color, and accessibility-first design systems.\n- Navigation Compose: Type-safe screen navigation and deep linking.\n\n2. State & Concurrency:\n- Kotlin Coroutines: Lightweight concurrency for asynchronous tasks.\n- Kotlin Flow (`StateFlow`, `SharedFlow`): Asynchronous reactive streams supporting UDF.\n- Architecture Components (`ViewModel`, `SavedStateHandle`): Separating business state from UI lifecycles.\n\n3. Data & Networking Layer:\n- Retrofit + OkHttp: Type-safe REST client with interceptors for authentication, logging, and retries.\n- KotlinX Serialization / Moshi: Fast, reflection-less JSON parsing.\n- Room Database: Robust SQLite object mapping with Flow/Paging 3 support.\n- Jetpack DataStore (Preferences / Proto): Modern, thread-safe asynchronous replacement for `SharedPreferences`.\n\n4. Dependency Injection:\n- Hilt (Dagger): Standardized compile-time dependency injection across Android components (`@AndroidEntryPoint`, `@HiltViewModel`).\n\n5. Asynchronous Work & Quality:\n- WorkManager: Guaranteed, deferrable background tasks with constraint management (battery, network).\n- Testing: JUnit 5, MockK, Turbine (for Flow testing), and Compose UI Test Framework.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA modern production Android application leverages the official Jetpack Modern Android Development (MAD) ecosystem, centered around Clean Architecture and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF):\n\n1. UI Layer:\n- Jetpack Compose: Modern declarative UI framework replacing imperative XML layouts. Enables reusable, reactive composables.\n- Material 3: Adaptive theming, dynamic color, and accessibility-first design systems.\n- Navigation Compose: Type-safe screen navigation and deep linking.\n\n2. State & Concurrency:\n- Kotlin Coroutines: Lightweight concurrency for asynchronous tasks.\n- Kotlin Flow (`StateFlow`, `SharedFlow`): Asynchronous reactive streams supporting UDF.\n- Architecture Components (`ViewModel`, `SavedStateHandle`): Separating business state from UI lifecycles.\n\n3. Data & Networking Layer:\n- Retrofit + OkHttp: Type-safe REST client with interceptors for authentication, logging, and retries.\n- KotlinX Serialization / Moshi: Fast, reflection-less JSON parsing.\n- Room Database: Robust SQLite object mapping with Flow/Paging 3 support.\n- Jetpack DataStore (Preferences / Proto): Modern, thread-safe asynchronous replacement for `SharedPreferences`.\n\n4. Dependency Injection:\n- Hilt (Dagger): Standardized compile-time dependency injection across Android components (`@AndroidEntryPoint`, `@HiltViewModel`).\n\n5. Asynchronous Work & Quality:\n- WorkManager: Guaranteed, deferrable background tasks with constraint management (battery, network).\n- Testing: JUnit 5, MockK, Turbine (for Flow testing), and Compose UI Test Framework.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// Modern stack integration: Hilt + Compose + ViewModel + StateFlow + Repository\n\n// 1. Domain/UI State\ndata class UserFeedUiState(\n    val items: List<String> = emptyList(),\n    val isLoading: Boolean = false,\n    val errorMessage: String? = null\n)\n\n// 2. Hilt ViewModel with StateFlow\n@HiltViewModel\nclass FeedViewModel @Inject constructor(\n    private val userRepository: UserRepository\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow(UserFeedUiState(isLoading = true))\n    val uiState: StateFlow<UserFeedUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()\n\n    init {\n        loadFeed()\n    }\n\n    fun loadFeed() {\n        viewModelScope.launch {\n            _uiState.update { it.copy(isLoading = true) }\n            userRepository.getFeed()\n                .onSuccess { data -> _uiState.update { it.copy(items = data, isLoading = false) } }\n                .onFailure { err -> _uiState.update { it.copy(errorMessage = err.localizedMessage, isLoading = false) } }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// 3. Declarative Jetpack Compose UI\n@Composable\nfun FeedScreen(\n    viewModel: FeedViewModel = hiltViewModel()\n) {\n    val state by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n\n    Box(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(), contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) {\n        when {\n            state.isLoading -> CircularProgressIndicator()\n            state.errorMessage != null -> Text(text = state.errorMessage!!, color = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.error)\n            else -> LazyColumn(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {\n                items(state.items) { item ->\n                    Text(text = item, modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp))\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
