    shortDescription:     "State-related bugs (e.g., race conditions, stale data, duplicate triggers, flickering UI, UI desync) almost always stem from two root causes:\n1. Multiple sources of truth competing with each other.\n2. Uncontrolled state ",
    explanation:     "State-related bugs (e.g., race conditions, stale data, duplicate triggers, flickering UI, UI desync) almost always stem from two root causes:\n1. Multiple sources of truth competing with each other.\n2. Uncontrolled state ",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nState-related bugs (e.g., race conditions, stale data, duplicate triggers, flickering UI, UI desync) almost always stem from two root causes:\n1. Multiple sources of truth competing with each other.\n2. Uncontrolled state mutation from asynchronous callbacks out of sync with the lifecycle.\n\nSystematic Diagnostic & Resolution Process:\n1. Identify the Single Source of Truth (SSOT): Ensure state is strictly held in one place (usually a `ViewModel` or local Room database). Views and Composables must be dumb renderers.\n2. Trace State Mutations: Use Kotlin `StateFlow` with atomic updates via `.update { it.copy(...) }` to prevent concurrent write race conditions.\n3. Verify Lifecycle Safety: Check whether collectors are running while the app is in the background. Use `repeatOnLifecycle` or Compose's `collectAsStateWithLifecycle`.\n4. Prevent Event Re-execution: Distinguish persistent state (like list of items) from one-time events (like navigation or Snackbars).\n5. Add Logging/Debugging: Attach log interceptors or wrap state changes with a debug logger to record every state transition.\n6. Write Deterministic Unit Tests: Use Turbine and `StandardTestDispatcher` to assert sequential state transitions.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nState-related bugs (e.g., race conditions, stale data, duplicate triggers, flickering UI, UI desync) almost always stem from two root causes:\n1. Multiple sources of truth competing with each other.\n2. Uncontrolled state mutation from asynchronous callbacks out of sync with the lifecycle.\n\nSystematic Diagnostic & Resolution Process:\n1. Identify the Single Source of Truth (SSOT): Ensure state is strictly held in one place (usually a `ViewModel` or local Room database). Views and Composables must be dumb renderers.\n2. Trace State Mutations: Use Kotlin `StateFlow` with atomic updates via `.update { it.copy(...) }` to prevent concurrent write race conditions.\n3. Verify Lifecycle Safety: Check whether collectors are running while the app is in the background. Use `repeatOnLifecycle` or Compose's `collectAsStateWithLifecycle`.\n4. Prevent Event Re-execution: Distinguish persistent state (like list of items) from one-time events (like navigation or Snackbars).\n5. Add Logging/Debugging: Attach log interceptors or wrap state changes with a debug logger to record every state transition.\n6. Write Deterministic Unit Tests: Use Turbine and `StandardTestDispatcher` to assert sequential state transitions.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// Problematic Code (Buggy):\n// Multiple mutable variables mutated concurrently from different threads\nclass BuggyViewModel : ViewModel() {\n    var isLoading = false // race condition!\n    var items = mutableListOf<String>() // not thread-safe!\n}\n\n// RESOLUTION: Single Source of Truth with Atomic State Updates & MVI / UDF\ndata class ProductListUiState(\n    val items: List<String> = emptyList(),\n    val isLoading: Boolean = false,\n    val selectedId: String? = null,\n    val errorMessage: String? = null\n)\n\nclass RobustProductViewModel(\n    private val repository: ProductRepository\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow(ProductListUiState())\n    val uiState: StateFlow<ProductListUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()\n\n    fun selectProduct(id: String) {\n        // Atomic update prevents race conditions when rapid clicks occur\n        _uiState.update { currentState ->\n            currentState.copy(selectedId = id)\n        }\n    }\n\n    fun loadProducts() {\n        viewModelScope.launch {\n            _uiState.update { it.copy(isLoading = true, errorMessage = null) }\n            try {\n                val data = repository.getProducts()\n                _uiState.update { it.copy(items = data, isLoading = false) }\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                _uiState.update { it.copy(errorMessage = e.message, isLoading = false) }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
