    shortDescription:     "Robust networking in Android requires handling transient failures (poor connectivity, timeouts), protocol failures (HTTP 4xx/5xx), connectivity switches (WiFi to Cellular), and parsing errors gracefully. Architectural St",
    explanation:     "Robust networking in Android requires handling transient failures (poor connectivity, timeouts), protocol failures (HTTP 4xx/5xx), connectivity switches (WiFi to Cellular), and parsing errors gracefully. Architectural St",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nRobust networking in Android requires handling transient failures (poor connectivity, timeouts), protocol failures (HTTP 4xx/5xx), connectivity switches (WiFi to Cellular), and parsing errors gracefully.\n\nArchitectural Strategy:\n1. Transport Layer (OkHttp):\n   - Configure reasonable timeouts (Connect: 15s, Read: 20s, Write: 20s).\n   - Add Retry Interceptors for idempotent operations (GET requests on 503/socket timeouts with exponential backoff).\n   - Connection Pooling and HTTP/2 multiplexing.\n2. Network Connectivity Monitoring:\n   - Use `ConnectivityManager.NetworkCallback` via a Flow to proactively listen to network capability changes (validate `NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET` and `NET_CAPABILITY_VALIDATED`).\n3. Domain Error Mapping:\n   - Never expose raw HTTP exceptions (`HttpException`, `SocketTimeoutException`) to the UI layer.\n   - Map exceptions into structured domain errors (`NetworkError.NoInternet`, `NetworkError.ServerError(code)`, `NetworkError.Timeout`).\n4. Offline Support & Caching:\n   - Cache-First architecture using Room database: UI observes Room Flow; network worker syncs data into Room.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nRobust networking in Android requires handling transient failures (poor connectivity, timeouts), protocol failures (HTTP 4xx/5xx), connectivity switches (WiFi to Cellular), and parsing errors gracefully.\n\nArchitectural Strategy:\n1. Transport Layer (OkHttp):\n   - Configure reasonable timeouts (Connect: 15s, Read: 20s, Write: 20s).\n   - Add Retry Interceptors for idempotent operations (GET requests on 503/socket timeouts with exponential backoff).\n   - Connection Pooling and HTTP/2 multiplexing.\n2. Network Connectivity Monitoring:\n   - Use `ConnectivityManager.NetworkCallback` via a Flow to proactively listen to network capability changes (validate `NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET` and `NET_CAPABILITY_VALIDATED`).\n3. Domain Error Mapping:\n   - Never expose raw HTTP exceptions (`HttpException`, `SocketTimeoutException`) to the UI layer.\n   - Map exceptions into structured domain errors (`NetworkError.NoInternet`, `NetworkError.ServerError(code)`, `NetworkError.Timeout`).\n4. Offline Support & Caching:\n   - Cache-First architecture using Room database: UI observes Room Flow; network worker syncs data into Room.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// 1. Domain Error Abstraction\nsealed interface AppResult<out T> {\n    data class Success<out T>(val data: T) : AppResult<T>\n    data class Failure(val error: DomainNetworkError) : AppResult<Nothing>\n}\n\nsealed interface DomainNetworkError {\n    object NoInternet : DomainNetworkError\n    object Timeout : DomainNetworkError\n    data class ServerError(val code: Int, val message: String?) : DomainNetworkError\n    data class Unknown(val throwable: Throwable) : DomainNetworkError\n}\n\n// 2. Safe API Call Utility Function\nsuspend fun <T> safeApiCall(apiCall: suspend () -> T): AppResult<T> {\n    return try {\n        AppResult.Success(apiCall())\n    } catch (e: UnknownHostException) {\n        AppResult.Failure(DomainNetworkError.NoInternet)\n    } catch (e: SocketTimeoutException) {\n        AppResult.Failure(DomainNetworkError.Timeout)\n    } catch (e: HttpException) {\n        AppResult.Failure(DomainNetworkError.ServerError(e.code(), e.message()))\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\n        if (e is CancellationException) throw e // MUST rethrow cancellation for coroutines!\n        AppResult.Failure(DomainNetworkError.Unknown(e))\n    }\n}\n\n// 3. Network Repository Implementation\nclass OrdersRepository(\n    private val ordersApi: OrdersApiService\n) {\n    suspend fun getOrders(): AppResult<List<Order>> {\n        return safeApiCall {\n            ordersApi.fetchOrders().map { it.toDomain() }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
