    shortDescription:     "A Log Interceptor is an OkHttp middleware component that intercepts outgoing HTTP requests before they hit the wire and incoming HTTP responses before they are returned to application code. It sits in OkHttp\u2019s chain of r",
    explanation:     "A Log Interceptor is an OkHttp middleware component that intercepts outgoing HTTP requests before they hit the wire and incoming HTTP responses before they are returned to application code. It sits in OkHttp\u2019s chain of r",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA Log Interceptor is an OkHttp middleware component that intercepts outgoing HTTP requests before they hit the wire and incoming HTTP responses before they are returned to application code. It sits in OkHttp\u2019s chain of responsibility (`Interceptor.Chain`).\n\nUse Cases:\n1. Observability & Debugging: Logging request URLs, HTTP methods, headers, payload bodies, HTTP status codes, and execution latency.\n2. Security & Compliance (Crucial): Redacting sensitive authentication headers (`Authorization: Bearer ***`), cookies, API tokens, passwords, and Personal Identifiable Information (PII) like credit cards or SSNs.\n3. Performance Monitoring: Calculating request duration to identify slow endpoints.\n4. Conditional Environments: Activating verbose network logging (`HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BODY`) in Debug builds while completely disabling or stripping body logging in Release/Production builds to prevent memory bloat and security leaks.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA Log Interceptor is an OkHttp middleware component that intercepts outgoing HTTP requests before they hit the wire and incoming HTTP responses before they are returned to application code. It sits in OkHttp\u2019s chain of responsibility (`Interceptor.Chain`).\n\nUse Cases:\n1. Observability & Debugging: Logging request URLs, HTTP methods, headers, payload bodies, HTTP status codes, and execution latency.\n2. Security & Compliance (Crucial): Redacting sensitive authentication headers (`Authorization: Bearer ***`), cookies, API tokens, passwords, and Personal Identifiable Information (PII) like credit cards or SSNs.\n3. Performance Monitoring: Calculating request duration to identify slow endpoints.\n4. Conditional Environments: Activating verbose network logging (`HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BODY`) in Debug builds while completely disabling or stripping body logging in Release/Production builds to prevent memory bloat and security leaks.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\nclass NetworkModule {\n\n    fun createOkHttpClient(isDebug: Boolean): OkHttpClient {\n        val builder = OkHttpClient.Builder()\n            .connectTimeout(15, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n            .readTimeout(20, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n\n        // 1. Custom Logging & Redaction Interceptor\n        val customLoggingInterceptor = Interceptor { chain ->\n            val request = chain.request()\n            val startTime = System.nanoTime()\n\n            // Proceed with network call\n            val response = try {\n                chain.proceed(request)\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                Log.e(\"NetworkLog\", \"Request failed: ${request.method} ${request.url}\", e)\n                throw e\n            }\n\n            val tookMs = TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS.toMillis(System.nanoTime() - startTime)\n\n            if (isDebug) {\n                val sanitizedHeaders = request.headers.names().joinToString { name ->\n                    val value = if (name.equals(\"Authorization\", ignoreCase = true)) \"REDACTED\" else request.header(name)\n                    \"$name: $value\"\n                }\n                Log.d(\"NetworkLog\", \"--> ${request.method} ${request.url} ($sanitizedHeaders)\")\n                Log.d(\"NetworkLog\", \"<-- ${response.code} ${response.message} in ${tookMs}ms\")\n            }\n\n            response\n        }\n\n        builder.addInterceptor(customLoggingInterceptor)\n\n        // 2. Standard HttpLoggingInterceptor with redacted headers\n        if (isDebug) {\n            val logging = HttpLoggingInterceptor { message ->\n                Log.d(\"OkHttp\", message)\n            }.apply {\n                level = HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BODY\n                redactHeader(\"Authorization\")\n                redactHeader(\"Cookie\")\n                redactHeader(\"X-Api-Key\")\n            }\n            builder.addInterceptor(logging)\n        }\n\n        return builder.build()\n    }\n}\n```",
