    shortDescription:     "When making multiple concurrent API calls where all results are mandatory:\n1. Concurrency: The calls should execute concurrently (in parallel) using `async` rather than sequentially to minimize overall network latency ($",
    explanation:     "When making multiple concurrent API calls where all results are mandatory:\n1. Concurrency: The calls should execute concurrently (in parallel) using `async` rather than sequentially to minimize overall network latency ($",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nWhen making multiple concurrent API calls where all results are mandatory:\n1. Concurrency: The calls should execute concurrently (in parallel) using `async` rather than sequentially to minimize overall network latency ($T = \\max(t_1, t_2)$ instead of $t_1 + t_2$).\n2. Structured Concurrency & Failure Propagation:\n   - Use `coroutineScope { }` as the scoping function.\n   - In `coroutineScope`, if any child coroutine launched with `async` throws an exception, the scope fails immediately.\n   - It automatically cancels all other running sibling `async` jobs (saving device battery, memory, and backend bandwidth) and rethrows the exception to the caller.\n   - Do NOT use `supervisorScope` here because `supervisorScope` isolates child failures (allowing siblings to continue).\n   - Do NOT launch coroutines in `GlobalScope` or unbounded external scopes.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nWhen making multiple concurrent API calls where all results are mandatory:\n1. Concurrency: The calls should execute concurrently (in parallel) using `async` rather than sequentially to minimize overall network latency ($T = \\max(t_1, t_2)$ instead of $t_1 + t_2$).\n2. Structured Concurrency & Failure Propagation:\n   - Use `coroutineScope { }` as the scoping function.\n   - In `coroutineScope`, if any child coroutine launched with `async` throws an exception, the scope fails immediately.\n   - It automatically cancels all other running sibling `async` jobs (saving device battery, memory, and backend bandwidth) and rethrows the exception to the caller.\n   - Do NOT use `supervisorScope` here because `supervisorScope` isolates child failures (allowing siblings to continue).\n   - Do NOT launch coroutines in `GlobalScope` or unbounded external scopes.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\ndata class UserDashboard(\n    val profile: UserProfile,\n    val orders: List<Order>\n)\n\nclass DashboardRepository(\n    private val userApi: UserApiService,\n    private val ordersApi: OrdersApiService,\n    private val ioDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher = Dispatchers.IO\n) {\n\n    // Suspend function making concurrent calls; fails fast if either call fails\n    suspend fun getDashboardData(userId: String): UserDashboard = withContext(ioDispatcher) {\n        // coroutineScope enforces that if either deferred call fails, the other is cancelled immediately\n        coroutineScope {\n            val profileDeferred: Deferred<UserProfile> = async {\n                userApi.fetchUserProfile(userId)\n            }\n\n            val ordersDeferred: Deferred<List<Order>> = async {\n                ordersApi.fetchUserOrders(userId)\n            }\n\n            // Await both results concurrently\n            UserDashboard(\n                profile = profileDeferred.await(),\n                orders = ordersDeferred.await()\n            )\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ViewModel consuming the repository safely:\nclass DashboardViewModel(\n    private val repository: DashboardRepository\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow<DashboardUiState>(DashboardUiState.Loading)\n    val uiState: StateFlow<DashboardUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()\n\n    fun loadDashboard(userId: String) {\n        viewModelScope.launch {\n            _uiState.value = DashboardUiState.Loading\n            try {\n                val dashboard = repository.getDashboardData(userId)\n                _uiState.value = DashboardUiState.Success(dashboard)\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                // If userApi OR ordersApi throws an error, it is caught here\n                _uiState.value = DashboardUiState.Error(e.message ?: \"Failed to load dashboard\")\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
