    explanation:     "Multithreading and coroutine execution order questions evaluate your understanding of:\n1. Thread scheduling & dispatcher queues (`Dispatchers.Main`, `Dispatchers.Default`, `Dispatchers.Unconfined`).\n2. Immediate vs stand",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nMultithreading and coroutine execution order questions evaluate your understanding of:\n1. Thread scheduling & dispatcher queues (`Dispatchers.Main`, `Dispatchers.Default`, `Dispatchers.Unconfined`).\n2. Immediate vs standard dispatchers (`Dispatchers.Main` vs `Dispatchers.Main.immediate`).\n3. Suspension points (`yield()`, `delay()`) vs blocking calls (`join()`, `runBlocking()`).\n\nExample Code Snippet Analysis:\n```kotlin\nfun main() = runBlocking {\n    println(\"1\")\n    val job = launch {\n        println(\"2\")\n        yield()\n        println(\"3\")\n    }\n    println(\"4\")\n    job.join()\n    println(\"5\")\n}\n```\n\nExecution Walkthrough:\n1. `runBlocking` initiates on the current thread.\n2. `println(\"1\")` runs immediately -> Output: `1`.\n3. `launch` is called on the default dispatcher of `runBlocking`. The child coroutine is queued in the event loop, but the current block does NOT pause yet.\n4. `println(\"4\")` executes immediately -> Output: `4`.\n5. `job.join()` is called. This is a suspension point! The parent coroutine suspends until `job` completes, yielding the thread back to the event loop.\n6. The event loop picks up the queued child coroutine.\n7. The child coroutine executes `println(\"2\")` -> Output: `2`.\n8. The child coroutine calls `yield()`. It yields execution and puts itself back at the end of the dispatcher's queue.\n9. Since no other work is waiting in the event loop queue, the child coroutine is immediately resumed.\n10. `println(\"3\")` executes -> Output: `3`.\n11. The child coroutine completes.\n12. `job.join()` resumes in the parent coroutine.\n13. `println(\"5\")` executes -> Output: `5`.\n\nFinal Output:\n```\n1\n4\n2\n3\n5\n```",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nMultithreading and coroutine execution order questions evaluate your understanding of:\n1. Thread scheduling & dispatcher queues (`Dispatchers.Main`, `Dispatchers.Default`, `Dispatchers.Unconfined`).\n2. Immediate vs standard dispatchers (`Dispatchers.Main` vs `Dispatchers.Main.immediate`).\n3. Suspension points (`yield()`, `delay()`) vs blocking calls (`join()`, `runBlocking()`).\n\nExample Code Snippet Analysis:\n```kotlin\nfun main() = runBlocking {\n    println(\"1\")\n    val job = launch {\n        println(\"2\")\n        yield()\n        println(\"3\")\n    }\n    println(\"4\")\n    job.join()\n    println(\"5\")\n}\n```\n\nExecution Walkthrough:\n1. `runBlocking` initiates on the current thread.\n2. `println(\"1\")` runs immediately -> Output: `1`.\n3. `launch` is called on the default dispatcher of `runBlocking`. The child coroutine is queued in the event loop, but the current block does NOT pause yet.\n4. `println(\"4\")` executes immediately -> Output: `4`.\n5. `job.join()` is called. This is a suspension point! The parent coroutine suspends until `job` completes, yielding the thread back to the event loop.\n6. The event loop picks up the queued child coroutine.\n7. The child coroutine executes `println(\"2\")` -> Output: `2`.\n8. The child coroutine calls `yield()`. It yields execution and puts itself back at the end of the dispatcher's queue.\n9. Since no other work is waiting in the event loop queue, the child coroutine is immediately resumed.\n10. `println(\"3\")` executes -> Output: `3`.\n11. The child coroutine completes.\n12. `job.join()` resumes in the parent coroutine.\n13. `println(\"5\")` executes -> Output: `5`.\n\nFinal Output:\n```\n1\n4\n2\n3\n5\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.*\n\nfun main() = runBlocking {\n    println(\"1 - Main starts\")\n\n    val job = launch {\n        println(\"2 - Inside child coroutine before yield\")\n        yield() // Cooperatively yields thread\n        println(\"3 - Inside child coroutine after yield\")\n    }\n\n    println(\"4 - Main after launching child\")\n    job.join() // Suspend until child completes\n    println(\"5 - Main finishes after child join\")\n}\n```",
