    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nWhen explaining technical decisions, use the **STAR + Trade-off Framework** (Situation, Task, Decision, Trade-offs Considered, Measurable Impact):\n\nExample Structure:\n1. Context & Problem: Describe the real business or engineering problem (e.g., slow build times, UI state bugs, bad crash rates).\n2. Architectural Decision:\n   - Declarative UI: Migrated from XML/ViewBinding to Jetpack Compose.\n   - Concurrency & Reactive Streams: Standardized on Kotlin Coroutines and StateFlow over RxJava/LiveData.\n   - Persistence: Replaced SharedPreferences with Proto DataStore for type safety and thread safety.\n   - Dependency Injection: Adopted Hilt for compile-time verified modular dependency injection.\n3. Trade-offs Evaluated:\n   - Example: Migrating to Jetpack Compose increased initial compiler build times and required teaching the team declarative patterns, but reduced boilerplate code by 40% and virtually eliminated UI synchronization bugs.\n4. Measurable Outcome:\n   - Reduced crash-free users from 97.5% to 99.8%.\n   - Cut feature development cycle time from 2 sprints to 1 sprint.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nWhen explaining technical decisions, use the **STAR + Trade-off Framework** (Situation, Task, Decision, Trade-offs Considered, Measurable Impact):\n\nExample Structure:\n1. Context & Problem: Describe the real business or engineering problem (e.g., slow build times, UI state bugs, bad crash rates).\n2. Architectural Decision:\n   - Declarative UI: Migrated from XML/ViewBinding to Jetpack Compose.\n   - Concurrency & Reactive Streams: Standardized on Kotlin Coroutines and StateFlow over RxJava/LiveData.\n   - Persistence: Replaced SharedPreferences with Proto DataStore for type safety and thread safety.\n   - Dependency Injection: Adopted Hilt for compile-time verified modular dependency injection.\n3. Trade-offs Evaluated:\n   - Example: Migrating to Jetpack Compose increased initial compiler build times and required teaching the team declarative patterns, but reduced boilerplate code by 40% and virtually eliminated UI synchronization bugs.\n4. Measurable Outcome:\n   - Reduced crash-free users from 97.5% to 99.8%.\n   - Cut feature development cycle time from 2 sprints to 1 sprint.",
