    shortDescription:     "Modern Android architecture follows Google\u2019s Guide to App Architecture, adhering to Separation of Concerns and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF): 1. UI Layer (Presentation):\n   - Jetpack Compose: Renders UI based on state.\n",
    explanation:     "Modern Android architecture follows Google\u2019s Guide to App Architecture, adhering to Separation of Concerns and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF): 1. UI Layer (Presentation):\n   - Jetpack Compose: Renders UI based on state.\n",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nModern Android architecture follows Google\u2019s Guide to App Architecture, adhering to Separation of Concerns and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF):\n\n1. UI Layer (Presentation):\n   - Jetpack Compose: Renders UI based on state.\n   - ViewModel: Holds immutable `StateFlow<UiState>`, survives configuration changes, handles user interactions.\n2. Domain Layer (Optional but recommended for complex apps):\n   - Use Cases / Interactors: Encapsulates single units of business logic (e.g., `ValidateCheckoutUseCase`, `GetPersonalizedFeedUseCase`). Reusable across multiple ViewModels and keeps ViewModels clean.\n3. Data Layer:\n   - Repositories: Single source of truth. Coordinates data between remote network APIs and local databases (Room / DataStore).\n   - Data Sources: RemoteDataSource (Retrofit) and LocalDataSource (Room DAO).\n4. Cross-Cutting Concerns:\n   - Dependency Injection (Hilt): Provides loose coupling and seamless mockability for unit testing.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nModern Android architecture follows Google\u2019s Guide to App Architecture, adhering to Separation of Concerns and Unidirectional Data Flow (UDF):\n\n1. UI Layer (Presentation):\n   - Jetpack Compose: Renders UI based on state.\n   - ViewModel: Holds immutable `StateFlow<UiState>`, survives configuration changes, handles user interactions.\n2. Domain Layer (Optional but recommended for complex apps):\n   - Use Cases / Interactors: Encapsulates single units of business logic (e.g., `ValidateCheckoutUseCase`, `GetPersonalizedFeedUseCase`). Reusable across multiple ViewModels and keeps ViewModels clean.\n3. Data Layer:\n   - Repositories: Single source of truth. Coordinates data between remote network APIs and local databases (Room / DataStore).\n   - Data Sources: RemoteDataSource (Retrofit) and LocalDataSource (Room DAO).\n4. Cross-Cutting Concerns:\n   - Dependency Injection (Hilt): Provides loose coupling and seamless mockability for unit testing.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// 1. Data Layer: Repository implementing Single Source of Truth\nclass OfflineFirstArticleRepository @Inject constructor(\n    private val localDao: ArticleDao,\n    private val remoteApi: ArticleApiService\n) : ArticleRepository {\n\n    override fun getArticles(): Flow<List<Article>> = flow {\n        // Step 1: Emit cached articles from local database immediately\n        val cached = localDao.getAllArticles().map { it.toDomain() }\n        emit(cached)\n\n        // Step 2: Fetch latest from network and update cache\n        try {\n            val remoteArticles = remoteApi.fetchTopHeadlines()\n            localDao.insertArticles(remoteArticles.map { it.toEntity() })\n            // Step 3: Emit updated cached articles\n            emit(localDao.getAllArticles().map { it.toDomain() })\n        } catch (e: Exception) {\n            // Network failed, but user still sees cached data!\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// 2. Domain Layer: Use Case with single responsibility\nclass FormatArticleTitleUseCase @Inject constructor() {\n    operator fun invoke(article: Article): Article {\n        return article.copy(title = article.title.trim().replaceFirstChar { it.uppercase() })\n    }\n}\n\n// 3. UI Layer: ViewModel consuming Domain/Data\n@HiltViewModel\nclass NewsViewModel @Inject constructor(\n    private val repository: ArticleRepository,\n    private val formatTitle: FormatArticleTitleUseCase\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    val uiState: StateFlow<List<Article>> = repository.getArticles()\n        .map { list -> list.map { formatTitle(it) } }\n        .stateIn(\n            scope = viewModelScope,\n            started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n            initialValue = emptyList()\n        )\n}\n```",
