    shortDescription:     "An Application Not Responding (ANR) occurs when the Android main (UI) thread is blocked and unable to process incoming input events or lifecycle callbacks:\n- Input event dispatch timeout: UI does not respond to key or to",
    explanation:     "An Application Not Responding (ANR) occurs when the Android main (UI) thread is blocked and unable to process incoming input events or lifecycle callbacks:\n- Input event dispatch timeout: UI does not respond to key or to",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nAn Application Not Responding (ANR) occurs when the Android main (UI) thread is blocked and unable to process incoming input events or lifecycle callbacks:\n- Input event dispatch timeout: UI does not respond to key or touch events within 5 seconds.\n- BroadcastReceiver execution timeout: `BroadcastReceiver` does not finish within 10\u201320 seconds.\n- Service execution timeout: Foreground Service start not completed within time limits.\n\nRoot Causes:\n1. Performing disk I/O (Room, SharedPreferences, file writing) on `Dispatchers.Main`.\n2. Synchronous network calls or heavy JSON serialization on Main thread.\n3. Lock contention: Main thread waiting for a lock held by a background thread.\n4. Heavy view inflation or deep view hierarchy traversal.\n\nSystematic Solution:\n1. Diagnosis:\n   - Extract `/data/anr/traces.txt` via `adb bugreport` or inspect Android Vitals in Google Play Console.\n   - Trace the `main` thread stack trace to locate the exact blocked line.\n   - Use Android Studio Profiler (CPU trace / System Trace) to detect long frames.\n   - Enable `StrictMode` in debug builds (`detectDiskReads()`, `detectDiskWrites()`, `detectNetwork()`).\n2. Resolution:\n   - Offload heavy operations to background threads using Coroutines (`Dispatchers.IO` for I/O, `Dispatchers.Default` for CPU-heavy tasks).\n   - Replace `SharedPreferences.apply()` / `commit()` with Jetpack DataStore.\n   - Ensure main-safety in all repositories.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nAn Application Not Responding (ANR) occurs when the Android main (UI) thread is blocked and unable to process incoming input events or lifecycle callbacks:\n- Input event dispatch timeout: UI does not respond to key or touch events within 5 seconds.\n- BroadcastReceiver execution timeout: `BroadcastReceiver` does not finish within 10\u201320 seconds.\n- Service execution timeout: Foreground Service start not completed within time limits.\n\nRoot Causes:\n1. Performing disk I/O (Room, SharedPreferences, file writing) on `Dispatchers.Main`.\n2. Synchronous network calls or heavy JSON serialization on Main thread.\n3. Lock contention: Main thread waiting for a lock held by a background thread.\n4. Heavy view inflation or deep view hierarchy traversal.\n\nSystematic Solution:\n1. Diagnosis:\n   - Extract `/data/anr/traces.txt` via `adb bugreport` or inspect Android Vitals in Google Play Console.\n   - Trace the `main` thread stack trace to locate the exact blocked line.\n   - Use Android Studio Profiler (CPU trace / System Trace) to detect long frames.\n   - Enable `StrictMode` in debug builds (`detectDiskReads()`, `detectDiskWrites()`, `detectNetwork()`).\n2. Resolution:\n   - Offload heavy operations to background threads using Coroutines (`Dispatchers.IO` for I/O, `Dispatchers.Default` for CPU-heavy tasks).\n   - Replace `SharedPreferences.apply()` / `commit()` with Jetpack DataStore.\n   - Ensure main-safety in all repositories.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// 1. StrictMode setup in Application class for early development ANR detection\nclass App : Application() {\n    override fun onCreate() {\n        super.onCreate()\n        if (BuildConfig.DEBUG) {\n            StrictMode.setThreadPolicy(\n                StrictMode.ThreadPolicy.Builder()\n                    .detectDiskReads()\n                    .detectDiskWrites()\n                    .detectNetwork()\n                    .penaltyLog()\n                    .penaltyDeath() // Crash early in development when Main thread is abused!\n                    .build()\n            )\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// 2. Offloading blocking I/O to Dispatchers.IO\nclass ContactSyncRepository(\n    private val context: Context,\n    private val ioDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher = Dispatchers.IO\n) {\n\n    // Main-safe suspend function: safe to call from Dispatchers.Main\n    suspend fun parseAndSaveLargeVCard(uri: Uri): Int = withContext(ioDispatcher) {\n        // Disk I/O executed safely on IO thread pool, preventing ANR\n        context.contentResolver.openInputStream(uri)?.use { stream ->\n            val contacts = parseStream(stream)\n            saveToRoomDatabase(contacts)\n            contacts.size\n        } ?: 0\n    }\n\n    private fun parseStream(stream: InputStream): List<String> = emptyList()\n    private fun saveToRoomDatabase(items: List<String>) {}\n}\n```",
