    shortDescription:     "Modern Android architecture combines these four technologies to form a reactive, unidirectional system:\n1. Kotlin Coroutines: Concurrency engine for executing one-shot asynchronous tasks without blocking threads.\n2. Kotl",
    explanation:     "Modern Android architecture combines these four technologies to form a reactive, unidirectional system:\n1. Kotlin Coroutines: Concurrency engine for executing one-shot asynchronous tasks without blocking threads.\n2. Kotl",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nModern Android architecture combines these four technologies to form a reactive, unidirectional system:\n1. Kotlin Coroutines: Concurrency engine for executing one-shot asynchronous tasks without blocking threads.\n2. Kotlin Flow: Reactive data stream engine for asynchronous sequences of data over time (cold streams like Room database emissions, hot streams like `StateFlow`).\n3. Jetpack Compose: Declarative UI engine that observes reactive state and draws UI without XML.\n4. MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel): Architectural separation where:\n   - Model (Data Layer): Exposes data streams via Flow.\n   - ViewModel: Collects Model streams, handles business events, and exposes an immutable `StateFlow<UiState>`.\n   - View (Compose): Observes `StateFlow` via `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` and renders UI.\n\nData and Event Flow:\n- User interacts with Compose UI -> Triggers lambda event in ViewModel -> ViewModel runs Coroutine -> Updates StateFlow -> Compose UI recomposes automatically.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nModern Android architecture combines these four technologies to form a reactive, unidirectional system:\n1. Kotlin Coroutines: Concurrency engine for executing one-shot asynchronous tasks without blocking threads.\n2. Kotlin Flow: Reactive data stream engine for asynchronous sequences of data over time (cold streams like Room database emissions, hot streams like `StateFlow`).\n3. Jetpack Compose: Declarative UI engine that observes reactive state and draws UI without XML.\n4. MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel): Architectural separation where:\n   - Model (Data Layer): Exposes data streams via Flow.\n   - ViewModel: Collects Model streams, handles business events, and exposes an immutable `StateFlow<UiState>`.\n   - View (Compose): Observes `StateFlow` via `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` and renders UI.\n\nData and Event Flow:\n- User interacts with Compose UI -> Triggers lambda event in ViewModel -> ViewModel runs Coroutine -> Updates StateFlow -> Compose UI recomposes automatically.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// MODEL\ndata class CryptoPrice(val symbol: String, val price: Double)\n\nclass CryptoRepository @Inject constructor() {\n    // Flow emitting live price updates every 2 seconds\n    fun getLivePrices(): Flow<List<CryptoPrice>> = flow {\n        while (true) {\n            emit(fetchFromNetwork())\n            delay(2000)\n        }\n    }.flowOn(Dispatchers.IO)\n\n    private fun fetchFromNetwork(): List<CryptoPrice> = listOf(CryptoPrice(\"BTC\", 65000.0))\n}\n\n// VIEWMODEL\ndata class CryptoUiState(\n    val prices: List<CryptoPrice> = emptyList(),\n    val isLoading: Boolean = false\n)\n\n@HiltViewModel\nclass CryptoViewModel @Inject constructor(\n    private val repository: CryptoRepository\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    val uiState: StateFlow<CryptoUiState> = repository.getLivePrices()\n        .map { CryptoUiState(prices = it, isLoading = false) }\n        .stateIn(\n            scope = viewModelScope,\n            started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n            initialValue = CryptoUiState(isLoading = true)\n        )\n}\n\n// COMPOSE VIEW\n@Composable\nfun CryptoPriceScreen(viewModel: CryptoViewModel = hiltViewModel()) {\n    val state by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n\n    if (state.isLoading) {\n        CircularProgressIndicator()\n    } else {\n        LazyColumn {\n            items(state.prices) { crypto ->\n                Text(\"${crypto.symbol}: $${crypto.price}\", modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp))\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
