    shortDescription:     "Both `StateFlow` and `SharedFlow` are \"Hot\" flows (they emit data regardless of whether collectors are active), but they serve fundamentally different architectural roles: 1. StateFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents persistent U",
    explanation:     "Both `StateFlow` and `SharedFlow` are \"Hot\" flows (they emit data regardless of whether collectors are active), but they serve fundamentally different architectural roles: 1. StateFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents persistent U",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nBoth `StateFlow` and `SharedFlow` are \"Hot\" flows (they emit data regardless of whether collectors are active), but they serve fundamentally different architectural roles:\n\n1. StateFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents persistent UI State (e.g., loading state, user profile, list of products).\n- Characteristics:\n  - Always holds a current `.value`.\n  - Conflated: If state updates rapidly (e.g., 1 -> 2 -> 3), a slow collector may skip intermediate values and receive only the latest value (3).\n  - Replay Cache = 1: Any new collector immediately receives the current latest state upon subscribing.\n  - Equality check: `StateFlow` checks `Any.equals()`. Emitting the identical value consecutively does NOT trigger collectors.\n\n2. SharedFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents Broadcast Events or one-off actions (e.g., navigation events, showing a temporary Toast/Snackbar, triggering an analytics beacon).\n- Characteristics:\n  - Does NOT require an initial value.\n  - Configurable `replay`: Can be set to 0 (new subscribers only receive events emitted *after* they subscribed).\n  - Buffer overflow strategies: `BufferOverflow.DROP_OLDEST`, `DROP_LATEST`, or `SUSPEND`.\n  - Emits all events: No conflation by default; every emission is delivered.\n\nDecision Matrix:\n- Screen State -> Use `StateFlow`.\n- Navigation / Transient Notification -> Use `SharedFlow` (with `replay = 0`) or Channel.",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nBoth `StateFlow` and `SharedFlow` are \"Hot\" flows (they emit data regardless of whether collectors are active), but they serve fundamentally different architectural roles:\n\n1. StateFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents persistent UI State (e.g., loading state, user profile, list of products).\n- Characteristics:\n  - Always holds a current `.value`.\n  - Conflated: If state updates rapidly (e.g., 1 -> 2 -> 3), a slow collector may skip intermediate values and receive only the latest value (3).\n  - Replay Cache = 1: Any new collector immediately receives the current latest state upon subscribing.\n  - Equality check: `StateFlow` checks `Any.equals()`. Emitting the identical value consecutively does NOT trigger collectors.\n\n2. SharedFlow:\n- Purpose: Represents Broadcast Events or one-off actions (e.g., navigation events, showing a temporary Toast/Snackbar, triggering an analytics beacon).\n- Characteristics:\n  - Does NOT require an initial value.\n  - Configurable `replay`: Can be set to 0 (new subscribers only receive events emitted *after* they subscribed).\n  - Buffer overflow strategies: `BufferOverflow.DROP_OLDEST`, `DROP_LATEST`, or `SUSPEND`.\n  - Emits all events: No conflation by default; every emission is delivered.\n\nDecision Matrix:\n- Screen State -> Use `StateFlow`.\n- Navigation / Transient Notification -> Use `SharedFlow` (with `replay = 0`) or Channel.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\nsealed interface NavigationEvent {\n    data class NavigateToDetails(val productId: String) : NavigationEvent\n}\n\ndata class ShopUiState(\n    val items: List<String> = emptyList(),\n    val isLoading: Boolean = false\n)\n\nclass ShopViewModel : ViewModel() {\n\n    // 1. StateFlow for persistent UI state\n    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow(ShopUiState(isLoading = true))\n    val uiState: StateFlow<ShopUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()\n\n    // 2. SharedFlow for one-time broadcast events (replay = 0 ensures no repeat on config change)\n    private val _eventFlow = MutableSharedFlow<NavigationEvent>(replay = 0)\n    val eventFlow: SharedFlow<NavigationEvent> = _eventFlow.asSharedFlow()\n\n    fun onProductClicked(id: String) {\n        viewModelScope.launch {\n            // Emits navigation event to collector\n            _eventFlow.emit(NavigationEvent.NavigateToDetails(id))\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// In Fragment/Activity:\nclass ShopActivity : AppCompatActivity() {\n    private val viewModel: ShopViewModel by viewModels()\n\n    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {\n        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)\n\n        // Collecting Events\n        lifecycleScope.launch {\n            repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED) {\n                viewModel.eventFlow.collect { event ->\n                    when (event) {\n                        is NavigationEvent.NavigateToDetails -> {\n                            // Navigate to details screen once!\n                            openDetails(event.productId)\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    private fun openDetails(id: String) {}\n}\n```",
