    shortDescription:     "An Android `Service` is a lifecycle-governed component that runs on the **Main thread** by default. To execute asynchronous background tasks safely inside a Service without memory leaks or orphaned threads, you must mana",
    explanation:     "An Android `Service` is a lifecycle-governed component that runs on the **Main thread** by default. To execute asynchronous background tasks safely inside a Service without memory leaks or orphaned threads, you must mana",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nAn Android `Service` is a lifecycle-governed component that runs on the **Main thread** by default. To execute asynchronous background tasks safely inside a Service without memory leaks or orphaned threads, you must manage a custom `CoroutineScope` following structured concurrency.\n\nArchitecture Requirements:\n1. Lifecycle-bound Scope: The scope must be created with a `SupervisorJob()` so individual task failures don't kill the entire Service prematurely.\n2. Context Composition: Combine `SupervisorJob()` with an appropriate dispatcher (e.g., `Dispatchers.Default` or `Dispatchers.IO`).\n3. Explicit Cancellation: When the Service is destroyed (`onDestroy()`), you MUST call `serviceScope.cancel()` to cleanly terminate all background jobs, preventing leaks of Service context.\n4. For Foreground Services: If doing long-running user-critical tasks (uploading, media playback, location tracking), show a persistent Notification and call `startForeground()` within Android OS time limits (under 10s on Android 12+).",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nAn Android `Service` is a lifecycle-governed component that runs on the **Main thread** by default. To execute asynchronous background tasks safely inside a Service without memory leaks or orphaned threads, you must manage a custom `CoroutineScope` following structured concurrency.\n\nArchitecture Requirements:\n1. Lifecycle-bound Scope: The scope must be created with a `SupervisorJob()` so individual task failures don't kill the entire Service prematurely.\n2. Context Composition: Combine `SupervisorJob()` with an appropriate dispatcher (e.g., `Dispatchers.Default` or `Dispatchers.IO`).\n3. Explicit Cancellation: When the Service is destroyed (`onDestroy()`), you MUST call `serviceScope.cancel()` to cleanly terminate all background jobs, preventing leaks of Service context.\n4. For Foreground Services: If doing long-running user-critical tasks (uploading, media playback, location tracking), show a persistent Notification and call `startForeground()` within Android OS time limits (under 10s on Android 12+).\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\nclass FileSyncService : Service() {\n\n    // 1. Create lifecycle-bound CoroutineScope\n    private val serviceJob = SupervisorJob()\n    private val serviceScope = CoroutineScope(serviceJob + Dispatchers.IO)\n\n    override fun onBind(intent: Intent?): IBinder? = null\n\n    override fun onCreate() {\n        super.onCreate()\n        Log.d(\"FileSyncService\", \"Service created\")\n    }\n\n    override fun onStartCommand(intent: Intent?, flags: Int, startId: Int): Int {\n        val fileUrl = intent?.getStringExtra(\"FILE_URL\") ?: return START_NOT_STICKY\n\n        // 2. Launch background work in managed scope\n        serviceScope.launch {\n            try {\n                performDownload(fileUrl)\n            } catch (e: Exception) {\n                if (e is CancellationException) throw e\n                Log.e(\"FileSyncService\", \"Download failed\", e)\n            } finally {\n                // Stop service once task finishes (if appropriate)\n                stopSelf(startId)\n            }\n        }\n\n        return START_NOT_STICKY\n    }\n\n    private suspend fun performDownload(url: String) {\n        // Simulating heavy download\n        delay(3000)\n        Log.d(\"FileSyncService\", \"Downloaded $url\")\n    }\n\n    // 3. MANDATORY: Clean up and cancel all coroutines when Service is destroyed\n    override fun onDestroy() {\n        super.onDestroy()\n        serviceScope.cancel() // Cancels all child coroutines immediately!\n        Log.d(\"FileSyncService\", \"Service destroyed and scope cancelled\")\n    }\n}\n```",
