    shortDescription:     "Senior Android live coding interviews typically test three dimensions:\n1. Functional Kotlin transformations (Collections, sequence manipulation, grouping).\n2. Concurrency handling (Coroutines, Debouncing, Parallel async,",
    explanation:     "Senior Android live coding interviews typically test three dimensions:\n1. Functional Kotlin transformations (Collections, sequence manipulation, grouping).\n2. Concurrency handling (Coroutines, Debouncing, Parallel async,",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nSenior Android live coding interviews typically test three dimensions:\n1. Functional Kotlin transformations (Collections, sequence manipulation, grouping).\n2. Concurrency handling (Coroutines, Debouncing, Parallel async, Mutex).\n3. Defensive production design (Error handling, immutability, thread-safety).\n\nCommon Senior Coding Problem Pattern:\n\"Implement an in-memory caching repository with a debounce search mechanism that makes concurrent network calls, merges results, and handles thread-safe cache updates.\"\n\nKey Senior Coding Habits to Demonstrate:\n- Clarify edge cases before writing code (null values, network failures, empty queries).\n- Use `StateFlow` / `Flow` with operators like `debounce()`, `distinctUntilChanged()`, and `flatMapLatest()`.\n- Use `Mutex` or atomic references if synchronization is required.\n- Ensure proper dispatcher management (`Dispatchers.IO`).",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nSenior Android live coding interviews typically test three dimensions:\n1. Functional Kotlin transformations (Collections, sequence manipulation, grouping).\n2. Concurrency handling (Coroutines, Debouncing, Parallel async, Mutex).\n3. Defensive production design (Error handling, immutability, thread-safety).\n\nCommon Senior Coding Problem Pattern:\n\"Implement an in-memory caching repository with a debounce search mechanism that makes concurrent network calls, merges results, and handles thread-safe cache updates.\"\n\nKey Senior Coding Habits to Demonstrate:\n- Clarify edge cases before writing code (null values, network failures, empty queries).\n- Use `StateFlow` / `Flow` with operators like `debounce()`, `distinctUntilChanged()`, and `flatMapLatest()`.\n- Use `Mutex` or atomic references if synchronization is required.\n- Ensure proper dispatcher management (`Dispatchers.IO`).\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// Problem: Build a Thread-Safe Search Repository with Debounce and In-Memory Cache\n\ndata class SearchResult(val query: String, val results: List<String>)\n\ninterface SearchApi {\n    suspend fun search(query: String): List<String>\n}\n\nclass SearchRepository(\n    private val api: SearchApi,\n    private val ioDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher = Dispatchers.IO\n) {\n    // Thread-safe in-memory cache protected by Mutex\n    private val cache = mutableMapOf<String, List<String>>()\n    private val mutex = Mutex()\n\n    suspend fun search(query: String): List<String> = withContext(ioDispatcher) {\n        val trimmedQuery = query.trim()\n        if (trimmedQuery.isEmpty()) return@withContext emptyList()\n\n        // 1. Check cache with thread-safe lock\n        mutex.withLock {\n            cache[trimmedQuery]?.let {\n                return@withContext it\n            }\n        }\n\n        // 2. Fetch from network\n        val networkResults = api.search(trimmedQuery)\n\n        // 3. Update cache thread-safely\n        mutex.withLock {\n            cache[trimmedQuery] = networkResults\n        }\n\n        networkResults\n    }\n}\n\n// In ViewModel: Reactive debounce pipeline\nclass SearchViewModel(\n    private val repository: SearchRepository\n) : ViewModel() {\n\n    private val searchQuery = MutableStateFlow(\"\")\n\n    val searchResults: StateFlow<List<String>> = searchQuery\n        .debounce(300) // Wait 300ms after user stops typing\n        .filter { it.isNotBlank() }\n        .distinctUntilChanged() // Ignore if same query emitted\n        .flatMapLatest { query ->\n            flow {\n                emit(repository.search(query))\n            }\n        }\n        .flowOn(Dispatchers.IO)\n        .stateIn(\n            scope = viewModelScope,\n            started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n            initialValue = emptyList()\n        )\n\n    fun onQueryChanged(newQuery: String) {\n        searchQuery.value = newQuery\n    }\n}\n```",
