    question:     "How would you review or reason about networking code and logging in an Android application?",
    slug:     "android-30-how-would-you-review-or-reason-about-networking-code-and-logging-in-an-android-application",
    categoryName:     "Android",
    categorySlug:     "android",
    subcategoryName:     "Android Development",
    subcategorySlug:     "android-development",
    experienceLevel:     "EXPERIENCED",
    difficulty:     "HARD",
    interviewType:     "TECHNICAL",
    shortDescription:     "A Senior Android Developer reviewing networking and logging pull requests evaluates the code across five critical pillars: 1. Architecture & Thread Safety:\n   - Is networking isolated in a Remote Data Source?\n   - Are su",
    explanation:     "A Senior Android Developer reviewing networking and logging pull requests evaluates the code across five critical pillars: 1. Architecture & Thread Safety:\n   - Is networking isolated in a Remote Data Source?\n   - Are su",
    sampleAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA Senior Android Developer reviewing networking and logging pull requests evaluates the code across five critical pillars:\n\n1. Architecture & Thread Safety:\n   - Is networking isolated in a Remote Data Source?\n   - Are suspend functions main-safe (e.g., using `Dispatchers.IO` or relying on Retrofit\u2019s native suspend execution)?\n   - Are domain models separated from network DTOs?\n\n2. Security & Compliance (Non-negotiable):\n   - Certificate Pinning: Is `CertificatePinner` configured for sensitive payment/auth endpoints?\n   - Cleartext Traffic: Is HTTP strictly banned in `network_security_config.xml`?\n   - Log Redaction: Are headers (`Authorization`, `Cookie`, `X-Auth-Token`) and sensitive fields (passwords, card CVVs) completely redacted in logs?\n   - Release Builds: Are logging interceptors strictly disabled or limited to error status codes in Release builds?\n\n3. Resilience & Failure Modes:\n   - Are timeouts configured properly (Connect, Read, Write)?\n   - Does error handling respect Coroutines cancellation (`CancellationException` must be rethrown)?\n   - Is there backoff on retries to avoid overwhelming backends during outages?\n\n4. Bandwidth & Performance:\n   - Is HTTP response caching enabled with `Cache-Control`?\n   - Are large payloads compressed using GZIP?",
    detailedAnswer:     "**Answer:**\n\nA Senior Android Developer reviewing networking and logging pull requests evaluates the code across five critical pillars:\n\n1. Architecture & Thread Safety:\n   - Is networking isolated in a Remote Data Source?\n   - Are suspend functions main-safe (e.g., using `Dispatchers.IO` or relying on Retrofit\u2019s native suspend execution)?\n   - Are domain models separated from network DTOs?\n\n2. Security & Compliance (Non-negotiable):\n   - Certificate Pinning: Is `CertificatePinner` configured for sensitive payment/auth endpoints?\n   - Cleartext Traffic: Is HTTP strictly banned in `network_security_config.xml`?\n   - Log Redaction: Are headers (`Authorization`, `Cookie`, `X-Auth-Token`) and sensitive fields (passwords, card CVVs) completely redacted in logs?\n   - Release Builds: Are logging interceptors strictly disabled or limited to error status codes in Release builds?\n\n3. Resilience & Failure Modes:\n   - Are timeouts configured properly (Connect, Read, Write)?\n   - Does error handling respect Coroutines cancellation (`CancellationException` must be rethrown)?\n   - Is there backoff on retries to avoid overwhelming backends during outages?\n\n4. Bandwidth & Performance:\n   - Is HTTP response caching enabled with `Cache-Control`?\n   - Are large payloads compressed using GZIP?\n\n**Example:**\n\n```kotlin\n// Production Code Review Standard: Secure, Resilient OkHttpClient Setup\n\nclass NetworkReviewStandards {\n\n    fun provideSecureOkHttpClient(\n        context: Context,\n        isDebug: Boolean\n    ): OkHttpClient {\n        val cacheSize = 10L * 1024 * 1024 // 10 MB Cache\n        val cache = Cache(File(context.cacheDir, \"http_cache\"), cacheSize)\n\n        return OkHttpClient.Builder()\n            .cache(cache)\n            .connectTimeout(15, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n            .readTimeout(20, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n            .writeTimeout(20, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\n            // 1. Certificate Pinning for sensitive banking/auth APIs\n            .certificatePinner(\n                CertificatePinner.Builder()\n                    .add(\"api.example.com\", \"sha256/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=\")\n                    .build()\n            )\n            // 2. Auth Interceptor adding tokens\n            .addInterceptor { chain ->\n                val original = chain.request()\n                val request = original.newBuilder()\n                    .header(\"Accept\", \"application/json\")\n                    .header(\"User-Agent\", \"Android-App-1.0\")\n                    .build()\n                chain.proceed(request)\n            }\n            // 3. Security-Compliant Logging Interceptor\n            .apply {\n                if (isDebug) {\n                    val loggingInterceptor = HttpLoggingInterceptor().apply {\n                        level = HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BODY\n                        redactHeader(\"Authorization\")\n                        redactHeader(\"Cookie\")\n                        redactHeader(\"Set-Cookie\")\n                    }\n                    addInterceptor(loggingInterceptor)\n                }\n            }\n            .build()\n    }\n}\n```",
